From a5b55d240c45d88ba3df95d1f5a7852e1b9e191f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:38:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add: Packages can say their interface fits a phone screen

A package declares a phone-sized interface with mobile = [[yes]] (or
mobile = true, or "yes"/"true" in any case) in config.lua, or through
setPackageInfo()/setModuleInfo(). The package exporter has a box that
writes the line and reads it back. getPackageConfig() now keeps a
boolean as "true"/"false" instead of dropping it; none of the 242
config.lua files in the package repository sets a top-level boolean,
so no repository package gains a detail.

Mudlet notes which packages' code made each label, mini console, user
window, command line, scroll box and text box, and which set the
borders, the main background image and the app and profile style
sheets. The owner walk passes over code no package owns, such as
Geyser's, so a Geyser widget is the package's that asked for it, and
over a library to the package that lists it in its dependencies. Code
compiled from a string counts as the profile's.

THeadlessSession exposes this as ScriptWindow::packages and
ScriptWindow::mobile, packageMobile(), profileLookPackages() and a
coalesced packageUiChanged signal, so Mudlet for Android and Mudlet
Web can leave out an undeclared package's interface on a small screen.
Desktop Mudlet shows everything as before; addCommand() is unchanged.

